==Russian==

===Etymology===
From [[Old East Slavic]] [[вѣдѣ]]. Russian [[ведь]] is a former [[Indo-European]] root [[perfect tense|perfect]] {{term/t|ine-pro|*wóyd-}} with [[mediopassive]] ending ''-ai'', with meaning "I have seen". Cognate with English [[wit]] (to wit).

===Pronunciation===
* {{audio|Ru-ведь.ogg|audio}}

===Interjection===
'''ведь''' (ved’)

# [[after all]]
# [[indeed]], [[surely]]
# [[why]], [[well]]
# [[then]], you know, you see
# isn’t it?
#:* {{lang|ru|Ведь [[уже#Russian|уже́]] [[поздно|по́здно]]}} — ''It’s late, isn’t it?''
#:* {{lang|ru|Ведь [[он#Russian|он]] [[знаток|знато́к]]}} — ''After all, he’s an expert.''
#:* {{lang|ru|Ведь [[я#Russian|я]] [[вы|вам]] [[говорить|говори́л]]!}} — ''But I told you!''

===Conjunction===
'''ведь''' (ved’)

# [[you see]], [[you know]]
#:* {{lang|ru|[[он#Russian|Он]] [[лежать|лежи́т]], ведь он [[на#Russian|на]] [[прошлый|про́шлой]] [[неделя#Russian|неде́ле]] [[заболевать|заболе́л]]}} — ''He’s in bed...he fell ill last week, you know.''

